      <h2>Essential Things to Pack</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Light, breathable clothing (linen or merino wool rather than synthetic fabrics in the heat)</li>
        <li>A light jacket or layer for the hill country (Nuwara Eliya can be genuinely cold at night)</li>
        <li>A sarong (doubles as temple cover-up, beach towel, picnic blanket)</li>
        <li>Wide-brimmed hat and high-SPF sunscreen</li>
        <li>Insect repellent (DEET-based for jungle and wildlife areas)</li>
        <li>Good walking sandals or shoes (many temple sites require extensive barefoot walking on hot stone)</li>
        <li>A small day pack and padlock for guesthouse lockers</li>
        <li>US dollar cash as a backup (widely accepted at major entry fees)</li>
        <li>Power adapters (Sri Lanka uses type D and G plugs, 230V)</li>
      </ul>

